        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 143 adds support for anchored container queries: see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5177580990496768\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5177580990496768</a>. Also see <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/anchored-container-queries\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/anchored-container-queries</a> for Chrome's blog post coverage.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds a guide to explain anchored container queries. Note that this is added underneath the CSS anchor positioning module page rather than containment, as that is where it is specced.</li>\n<li>Adds details of anchored container query syntax to the <code class=\"notranslate\">container-type</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> reference pages.</li>\n<li>Links to the guide and otherwise mentions the feature in appropriate places. (I may have missed some; let me know if you spot any other places where this should be mentioned).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42710",
            "title": "Technical review: Document anchored container queries",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-09T14:59:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-09T14:58:05.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169272761?u=216904e59fc878dca16fb27b4b0450d5e5b69120&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR clarifies the requirements for implementing thenables in the Promise documentation, explicitly noting that a thenable’s <code class=\"notranslate\">.then()</code> method must not be <code class=\"notranslate\">async</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A warning and example have been added to explain how using <code class=\"notranslate\">async</code> can cause thrown errors to escape Promise error handling, leading to unexpected behavior during Promise resolution.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Promise specification expects thenables to signal fulfillment or rejection synchronously, either by throwing or by explicitly calling the rejection handler. Using an <code class=\"notranslate\">async</code> function for <code class=\"notranslate\">.then()</code> violates this expectation because <code class=\"notranslate\">async</code> functions always wrap errors in a returned Promise.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change helps readers avoid subtle bugs when implementing custom thenables and aligns the documentation with the actual Promise resolution semantics.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42193.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3684084966\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42193\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42193/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42193\">#42193</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42709",
            "title": "Clarify that thenable .then() must not be async",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-09T15:05:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-09T14:54:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "MUSKANNISHAD",
                "url": "https://github.com/MUSKANNISHAD"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates guidance on <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;hr&gt;</code> styling:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Removes ambiguous “appropriate CSS”</li>\n<li>Adds reference to the <code class=\"notranslate\">border-style</code> CSS property</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To make it clearer what CSS can be used.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42363.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3722601732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42363\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42363/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42363\">#42363</a></p>",
