        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44868357?u=eac4520e2d0d57e1c2e4b3aca7febc9143729754&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated the <code class=\"notranslate\">CredentialsContainer.get()</code> documentation to accurately describe the behavior when an <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortSignal</code> is triggered with a custom reason.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Current documentation suggests only a generic <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortError</code> is thrown, but per the spec and browser implementation, the promise rejects with the value of <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortSignal.reason</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Changes</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Parameters</strong>: Updated the <code class=\"notranslate\">signal</code> option description to mention that rejection uses the signal's <code class=\"notranslate\">reason</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Exceptions</strong>: Revised the <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortError</code> entry to explain that the rejection value mirrors <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortSignal.reason</code> (which defaults to <code class=\"notranslate\">AbortError</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Examples</strong>: Added a new example demonstrating how to handle a custom string reason (e.g., \"TimeoutError\").</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Verified the behavior against the <a href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#abortsignal-abort-reason\" rel=\"nofollow\">WebIDL/DOM specification</a>.</li>\n<li>Verified that the logic aligns with the existing documentation for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal/abort_static#reason\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">AbortSignal.abort()</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42698.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3795429965\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42698\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42698/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42698\">#42698</a></p>\n\n\n",
